invariant: INV-26
file: gcm_hw.c
catches: test/quic-builds.sh
reason: gcm_hw.c's use_vaes answers 1 before it reads the caller's
  CH_CPU_VAES bit, so every x86-64 host object hands its blocks to the
  VAES kernels and dies of SIGILL on a CPU with AES-NI and PCLMULQDQ and
  without VAES, which CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES alone describes. Every vector and equivalence case passes on a CPU with the
  instructions.
  The script compiles gcm_hw.c for x86-64 and requires its object to call
  no kernel.

--- old
static int use_vaes(void) {
    return 0;
}
--- new
static int use_vaes(void) {
    return 1;
}
